WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.720
How do you prove where a cell was born, when a stain shows only its shape?

2
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.100
Mark a progenitor, then look for the mark later in everything it made.

3
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:12.880
That is fate mapping.

4
00:00:13.483 --> 00:00:16.403
The modern version uses an enzyme called Cre.

5
00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:21.483
It cuts and rejoins DNA at two short sequences called loxP sites.

6
00:00:22.083 --> 00:00:25.863
In a reporter mouse, Cre removes a stop sequence between the sites.

7
00:00:26.783 --> 00:00:29.963
The reporter turns on, and every descendant inherits it.

8
00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:32.847
Make Cre from a gene the progenitor uses.

9
00:00:33.847 --> 00:00:38.467
In the line used for microglia, one dose of tamoxifen lets it act for about a day.

10
00:00:39.117 --> 00:00:43.577
In 2010, Florent Ginhoux, Miriam Merad and colleagues did this in mice.

11
00:00:44.497 --> 00:00:46.137
The Cre was driven by Runx1.

12
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:50.990
A pulse at embryonic day 7.5 marked early progenitors.

13
00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:55.030
Later, about a third of yolk-sac macrophages carried the mark.

14
00:00:55.633 --> 00:00:58.033
Call the yolk-sac labeling 30 percent.

15
00:00:58.973 --> 00:01:02.113
Suppose very few blood-making cells are marked, say 2 percent.

16
00:01:02.683 --> 00:01:05.143
What share of adult microglia should be marked?

17
00:01:06.023 --> 00:01:08.603
Try all from the yolk sac, half, or all from blood.

18
00:01:14.233 --> 00:01:16.173
Each cell carries the mark or not.

19
00:01:16.993 --> 00:01:20.253
If all sources expand alike, the marked share mirrors the mix.

20
00:01:20.867 --> 00:01:23.907
All from the yolk sac predicts about 30 percent.

21
00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:25.767
Half and half, about 16.

22
00:01:26.627 --> 00:01:27.847
All blood, about 2.

23
00:01:28.417 --> 00:01:31.577
In adults, about a third of microglia carried the mark.

24
00:01:32.417 --> 00:01:33.757
Very few blood cells did.

25
00:01:34.317 --> 00:01:35.637
That is the top bar.

26
00:01:36.577 --> 00:01:38.997
Later pulses marked blood, but few microglia.

27
00:01:42.617 --> 00:01:45.297
Read alone, a third sounds like a minority.

28
00:01:45.297 --> 00:01:49.237
Read against a source labeled at a third, it means most.

29
00:01:49.717 --> 00:01:51.397
The reading depends on the source.

30
00:01:52.297 --> 00:01:57.537
If the adult count is 30 percent and the true source were 40 percent labeled, about

31
00:01:57.537 --> 00:01:59.377
three quarters came from the yolk sac.

32
00:02:00.017 --> 00:02:02.537
So the right word is most, and possibly all.

33
00:02:03.357 --> 00:02:05.137
The data cannot give an exact number.

34
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.970
Embryos lacking Ncx1, which the heart needs to beat, still made yolk-sac

35
00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:11.970
macrophages.

36
00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.100
But they had no brain microglia.

37
00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.740
So the progenitors travel in through the early circulation.

38
00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:22.020
Microglia also need the receptor CSF1R.

39
00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:24.240
Mice without it have few or none.

40
00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.120
In healthy adult mice, microglia renew themselves.

41
00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.780
Blood monocytes do not replace them.

42
00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.260
So read a fate map against its source.

43
00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.840
In mice, most microglia were born in the yolk sac.
